\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Conjugating the Clifford directions}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{On a field with the real product spin basis of \ref{fdip-00LB},
conjugation fixes every direction operator. In \ref{fdip-013T}
a second antiunitary negates them all. What does a different
choice of spin space allow? Can the traces of products of directions
detect which choice of sign is possible?}

\p{The coefficients of a spin field also carry an internal index
and a site label. How does a conjugation acting on the entire
field change the centered operator and its link transports?}

